  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 108 PM EDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nMain focus remains on near term as shower and thunderstorm activity \nshould slowly increase this afternoon into early evening ahead of a \nsfc front. A stronger storm developed over Lk MI and has been moving \nacross Van Buren into Kalamazoo counties in MI. Some attempt at \nfurther development SW is noted, but they are struggling due to a \nlack of upper support. The trough will continue east with a modest, \nyet marginally sufficient shear profile to allow for some increase in \nintensity with time. With the best lift remaining north, cells will \ntend to grow rather quickly, but then struggle to maintain \nthemselves outside of any storm or outflow interactions. Best window \nstill appears to be 19-20Z to maybe as late as 2Z. Locally damaging \nwinds, marginally severe hail (freezing levels rather high today) \nand a very low chance for an isolated brief tornado in the early \nstages of development. SWODY1 slight risk was maintained across most \nof the area. Flooding concerns appear very limited given expected \ncoverage and duration. \n\nAnother weak mid level trough will pass through during peak heating \nThursday afternoon. Some limited instability and moisture will still \nexist mainly across SE sections to bring a small chance for a shower \nor storm in the 20-24Z Thu time frame. Will continue with silent 14 \npops in these areas for now. \n\nThursday night through the weekend will feature a change in the \nupper level flow to more of a semi-zonal setup as another northern \nstream trough digs in the Pacific NW. As a result, dry and \nseasonably warm weather will settle in with highs in the 80s, lows \nin the 60s and somewhat elevated, but tolerable humidity values. The \naformentioned trough looks to move into the Dakotas by Monday, but \nthen be shunted NE as a 595 dm high across the SE U.S edges north. \nModel blend continues to throw in some token slgt chc pops as it \nstruggles with waves that pass nearby, but likely cause no real \nimpact.",
